rgin": -0.75, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.7, "baseline_margin": 0.57, "analyst_adjustment": -0.57, "key_factors": ["Ratings split between Tossup and Tilt/Lean R, with one outlier calling it Lean D", "September GBAO poll shows McCann up 1, but it's a single Democratic-sponsored survey", "Markets price Huizenga slightly ahead (roughly 53% Republican)", "Huizenga holds incumbency and fundraising advantages; outside groups are attacking him heavily"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a narrow Republican edge from the district's R+3 lean offset by a strong Democratic environment, while the lone recent poll shows a one-point McCann lead and markets tilt slightly to Huizenga. With expert ratings clustered at Tossup, the race sits essentially at even.", "watch": "Whether additional independent polling confirms McCann's September lead or Huizenga's incumbency and outside spending pull him back ahead.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Bill Huizenga (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Southwest Michigan's 4th District is one of the closest House races of 2026. Incumbent Republican Bill Huizenga faces Democratic state Senator Sean McCann in a district with a modest Republican lean, but a favorable national environment for Democrats has kept the contest tight. Huizenga has raised more than $4 million and holds a cash advantage, though outside groups have spent heavily attacking him, including ads questioning his stock-trading record.\n\nExpert ratings are split: most call the race a Tossup, while Cook and Decision Desk lean Republican and one outlet rates it a Democratic flip. A September Democratic-sponsored poll showed McCann ahead by a single point, and prediction markets give Huizenga a slight edge. With no clear signal in either direction, this race is rated a genuine tossup.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5309, "margin": 0.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4667, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4711, "margin"